with center of enlargement at the origin.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the shear, and let $Q$ be the matrix that represents the scaling. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $QP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =QP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b16f563c-f4be-5883-8734-cbce48de4757" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix That Represents a Combination of Three Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd7126f6-cb5d-5c9c-89e6-548689eb2f51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd7126f6-cb5d-5c9c-89e6-548689eb2f51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362854} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d04e494-40e1-5933-8305-0c99e51ebd93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e787fcb-e5a5-5c27-9e4a-eb8b79b0935a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e787fcb-e5a5-5c27-9e4a-eb8b79b0935a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362856} :answer-field/